            <ArticleTitle>Acute generalized exanthematous pustulosis caused by morphine, confirmed by positive patch test and lymphocyte transformation test.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S21-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Morphine, an opium alkaloid, frequently causes side effects such as hyperhidrosis and facial flushing, but serious cutaneous adverse drug reactions are seldom observed. Best known are urticaria, erythema, and pruritus; sometimes pseudoallergic anaphylactoid reactions, and blisters are reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
